From 64e8c41342d4e7f015a490c583113e9d395622c0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Xiaozhi & Tono AI Team <noreply>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 22:24:15 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] feat(webworker-runtime): let createWorkerHost install a VFS
 sink

A host that mirrors the Worker's in-memory filesystem must attach its
durable observer to the mounted MemoryVfs. The runtime already accepts a
VfsMutationSink in MemoryVfs options, but createWorkerHost builds the
filesystem itself, so a deployment had no seam to supply that sink before
boot and had to reach into the mounted instance afterwards.

Add `sink` to WorkerHostOptions and construct the mounted MemoryVfs with
it. The semantics are the ones MemoryVfs already fixes: image and overlay
seeding stay silent, every mutation committed afterwards reaches record()
without delaying its caller, and host.vfs.flush() settles the recorded work.
A sink that cannot persist reports the failure itself and stops mirroring
rather than rejecting a write that already committed.

Export VfsMutation, VfsMutationListener, and VfsMutationSink from the
package root so the option's callback shape is reachable without a deep
import.

Test: packages/experimental/webworker-runtime/tests/worker-host-sink.spec.ts
asserts the mounted filesystem carries the sink, seeding is silent, a write
reaches record(), and flush() settles the sink.
